1
00:00:14,147 --> 00:00:17,291
Following a card,
I found a place.

2
00:00:17,684 --> 00:00:21,221
When I stopped there,
it began to feel like home.

3
00:00:22,793 --> 00:00:25,936
Following my angel,
I came to you.

4
00:00:27,508 --> 00:00:30,652
When I was yang,
I searched for yin.

5
00:00:32,224 --> 00:00:35,761
Now that I am yin,
looking at you is enough.

6
00:00:40,869 --> 00:00:44,013
There was in her face
a quiet beauty,

7
00:00:44,406 --> 00:00:47,550
the kind that never asks
to be noticed.

8
00:00:48,729 --> 00:00:51,873
The depth of her eyes,
the line of her mouth,

9
00:00:52,266 --> 00:00:55,409
her hair arranged
with a care

10
00:00:55,802 --> 00:00:58,553
that accentuates
without correcting.

11
00:01:00,518 --> 00:01:02,876
And then she spoke.

12
00:01:03,269 --> 00:01:06,413
Brazil remained intact
in the way she spoke:

13
00:01:06,806 --> 00:01:09,557
the warm weight of the vowels,

14
00:01:09,950 --> 00:01:12,700
the lingering syllable,

15
00:01:13,093 --> 00:01:16,237
a music
that refused

16
00:01:16,630 --> 00:01:18,988
to disguise itself.

17
00:01:20,953 --> 00:01:24,097
Then I understood
that the light of that face

18
00:01:24,490 --> 00:01:27,240
was still missing
her voice.

19
00:01:29,598 --> 00:01:31,956
Then came
the embrace.

20
00:01:32,349 --> 00:01:35,493
I do not know how long it lasted

21
00:01:35,886 --> 00:01:38,637
or who moved closer first.

22
00:01:39,030 --> 00:01:41,780
I remember only
the warmth.

23
00:01:44,531 --> 00:01:47,675
And there remained as well
that private injustice

24
00:01:48,068 --> 00:01:50,819
memory sometimes commits:

25
00:01:51,212 --> 00:01:54,356
from an entire afternoon
it keeps intact

26
00:01:54,749 --> 00:01:56,714
a face,

27
00:01:57,892 --> 00:02:00,643
and from an entire embrace,

28
00:02:01,822 --> 00:02:03,787
the warmth.

29
00:02:09,682 --> 00:02:12,040
Before you smile,

30
00:02:12,432 --> 00:02:14,790
your eyes
have already stopped me.

31
00:02:15,969 --> 00:02:18,720
Under your gaze,

32
00:02:19,113 --> 00:02:21,864
the face I came in with
falls out of order.

33
00:02:23,829 --> 00:02:26,187
Your eyelids narrow.

34
00:02:27,759 --> 00:02:30,509
I do not know how much of me

35
00:02:30,902 --> 00:02:33,260
you have already seen.

36
00:02:34,439 --> 00:02:36,797
And I do not look away.

37
00:02:42,692 --> 00:02:45,049
I was going to tell you something.

38
00:02:46,621 --> 00:02:49,765
Your smile begins
at the corners of your mouth:

39
00:02:50,158 --> 00:02:52,909
the slightest movement,

40
00:02:53,302 --> 00:02:56,446
and I am already looking at you
beyond all caution.

41
00:02:58,411 --> 00:03:01,161
The gesture spreads
across your face.

42
00:03:01,554 --> 00:03:03,519
I smile too.

43
00:03:03,912 --> 00:03:06,270
You still have not said a word.

44
00:03:07,842 --> 00:03:09,807
I search for the sentence.

45
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:12,558
You smile again

46
00:03:12,951 --> 00:03:15,308
and I remain on your lips,

47
00:03:15,701 --> 00:03:18,059
never reaching the words.

48
00:03:22,775 --> 00:03:25,919
Black, with that sheen of a mane
that flashes when you turn your head:

49
00:03:26,312 --> 00:03:29,456
light glides across it
without ever making it lighter.

50
00:03:30,634 --> 00:03:33,385
It falls across your shoulder
and takes its time becoming still.

51
00:03:33,778 --> 00:03:36,136
You return to your words;

52
00:03:36,529 --> 00:03:39,280
but one strand prolongs
the turning of your face.

53
00:03:40,852 --> 00:03:43,603
You brush it aside
with your fingers.

54
00:03:43,996 --> 00:03:46,353
The gesture bares your neck

55
00:03:46,746 --> 00:03:49,497
and leaves between the strands
a crack of light.

56
00:03:51,069 --> 00:03:53,034
You let it go.

57
00:03:53,427 --> 00:03:55,785
The strand falls back into place.

58
00:03:56,178 --> 00:03:58,143
You keep talking.

59
00:04:02,072 --> 00:04:04,823
Your skin has that bronze tone.

60
00:04:05,216 --> 00:04:07,967
In the bend of your elbow
the colour deepens.

61
00:04:09,146 --> 00:04:11,897
The light lingers on your shoulder,

62
00:04:12,290 --> 00:04:14,648
travels down your arm

63
00:04:15,041 --> 00:04:17,791
and reaches the hand
that accompanies your voice.

64
00:04:19,363 --> 00:04:22,114
You move your fingers

65
00:04:22,507 --> 00:04:24,865
and a fleeting brightness
slides across your knuckles.

66
00:04:26,437 --> 00:04:28,402
My hand remains still.

67
00:04:29,974 --> 00:04:33,117
I would like to know that smoothness
with something more than my eyes:

68
00:04:33,510 --> 00:04:35,868
to lay my hand there slowly,

69
00:04:36,261 --> 00:04:38,226
leave it there,

70
00:04:38,619 --> 00:04:41,763
and feel your skin
gradually warming mine.

71
00:04:46,086 --> 00:04:48,836
I was going to write you a poem.

72
00:04:49,229 --> 00:04:51,194
You handed me an onion.

73
00:04:51,980 --> 00:04:53,552
—Start with this.

74
00:04:54,731 --> 00:04:57,482
Two minutes later
you had already made me cry

75
00:04:57,875 --> 00:05:00,233
without breaking my heart.

76
00:05:01,805 --> 00:05:04,555
You hum something in Portuguese
while the oil grows hot.

77
00:05:05,734 --> 00:05:08,092
I keep the rhythm with my foot.

78
00:05:09,664 --> 00:05:12,022
The spoon
goes still in my hand.

79
00:05:12,808 --> 00:05:14,380
—Stir, poet.

80
00:05:15,952 --> 00:05:18,703
I had forgotten about the stew.

81
00:05:19,095 --> 00:05:21,846
I was looking for a word
for the way you smile.

82
00:05:23,025 --> 00:05:24,990
You hold out the spoon.

83
00:05:25,383 --> 00:05:27,348
—Taste it. What does it need?

84
00:05:28,527 --> 00:05:30,492
I keep looking at you.

85
00:05:30,885 --> 00:05:32,457
—The stew, Paco.

86
00:05:33,243 --> 00:05:34,422
—Salt.

87
00:05:35,600 --> 00:05:37,958
You set out two plates.

88
00:05:38,351 --> 00:05:40,709
I carry the stew to the table.

89
00:05:41,102 --> 00:05:43,460
You move the papers aside
to make room for it.

90
00:05:45,032 --> 00:05:47,390
The poem is still unfinished.

91
00:05:48,962 --> 00:05:50,926
You ask me for the bread.

92
00:05:51,319 --> 00:05:52,891
I give you my hand.

93
00:05:53,677 --> 00:05:55,249
—The bread, poet.

94
00:05:56,035 --> 00:05:58,000
I reach for it with the other.
